; engine-strict is ON, so `npm install` HARD-FAILS on any package whose
; `engines.node` excludes the locked Node 14.15. That is the point: `engines` alone
; is advisory (npm warns and proceeds), which is what let the stack drift in the
; first place. See design/STACK-RECONCILIATION-PLAN.md §4 — this line is the second
; half of §4, left undone in June 2026 and turned on 2026-08-24. To-do item 4.7
; stays OPEN until the install described below actually verifies it.
;
; ⚠ UNVERIFIED UNTIL THE INSTALL RUNS. The three `overrides` below were chosen from
; a read-only registry check; no install has yet proved the resolved tree is clean.
; If `npm install` fails with EBADENGINE, that is this line doing its job — read the
; error, fix the offender with an override, and never "fix" it by setting this to
; false or by raising the Node target (CLAUDE.md, one-directional rule).
;
; WHAT THE OVERRIDES IN package.json ARE FOR. A scan of the installed tree on
; 2026-08-24 found SEVEN Node-engine mismatches, not the two recorded in June:
;   js-beautify 1.14.0   — clears minimatch@9, minipass@7, path-scurry, nopt@7,
;                          abbrev@2. All five arrived 2026-07-21 (`bbc476e`, the
;                          component-test tooling) via @vue/test-utils -> pretty ->
;                          js-beautify 1.15.4, whose glob@10 chain needs Node 14.17+.
;                          1.14.0 uses glob@7 + nopt@5 and declares node >=10.
;   @nuxt/telemetry      — SCOPED to consola only. 1.5.0 nests consola@3.4.2
;     { consola 2.15.3 }   (wants 14.18+); 2.15.3 is already the top-level version, so
;                          nothing new enters the tree. Deliberately scoped rather
;                          than downgrading the whole package to 1.3.6: that would
;                          pull defu@5.0.1, which carries a HIGH prototype-pollution
;                          advisory (GHSA-737v-mqg7-c878, affects <=6.1.4), replacing
;                          the patched defu@6.1.7 that 1.5.0 uses today.
;   node-releases 2.0.14 — 2.0.47 declares node >=18; 2.0.14 declares no engines.
;
; Node 14.15 and all runtime deps stay locked. Adding a dev tool that needs a newer
; Node is a Stack Constitution deviation and is logged on
; design/features/to-do-items.json the moment it is found — the five above were not,
; which is why this task was a month bigger than the list said.
engine-strict=true

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Playwright: NOBODY downloads a browser as a side effect of `npm install`.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; `playwright` ships an install script that fetches Chromium + Firefox + WebKit
; — measured at 604 MB — on EVERY machine that installs, including the master
; team's. That is not something to hand them silently (see design/ACTIONS.md 3.5,
; Carl's open npm-install question). This line suppresses that download for
; everyone; a developer who actually wants to run a visual check opts in with
;     npm run visual:setup      (Chromium only, ~265 MB)
; Verified 2026-08-21: the install then prints "Skipping browsers download ..."
; and adds two small text packages, and `visual:setup` afterwards still launches
; Chromium 114 from the locked Node 14.15.
;
; This also narrows GHSA-7mvr-c777-76hp (browser downloads skip TLS verification,
; unfixed below playwright 1.55.1, which requires Node 18 and so cannot be taken
; under the Node 14.15 lock). With this line the download step never runs at all
; except where a developer deliberately asks for it. See
; design/SECURITY-AUDIT-NOTES.md.
playwright_skip_browser_download=1
